---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="2DCAT | Dark Synthpop from Washington DC"
  description="2DCAT is a dark synthpop duo from Washington, D.C. Analog synthesizers, commanding vocals, and machine-driven rhythms rooted in darkwave, coldwave, and dark synthpop."
>
  <style>
    footer { display: none; }
    main { padding-top: 0; }

    .hero {
      position: relative;
      width: 100vw;
      height: 100vh;
      z-index: 1;
    }
    .hero-img {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center;
      z-index: 0;
    }
    .hero-overlay {
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      background: linear-gradient(to bottom, rgba(0,0,0,0.2) 0%, rgba(0,0,0,0.5) 100%);
      z-index: 1;
    }
    .hero-content {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 4rem;
      left: 2rem;
      z-index: 2;
    }
    header { z-index: 200; }

    .bio-section {
      background: #0a0a0a;
      padding: 5rem 2rem;
      max-width: 680px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    .bio-section p {
      font-size: 1rem;
      line-height: 1.8;
      color: #999;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
    .bio-section p:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
    .bio-section a {
      color: #CCC3B2;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(204,195,178,0.3);
      transition: border-color 0.2s;
    }
    .bio-section a:hover {
      border-bottom-color: #CCC3B2;
    }
    .sr-kw {
  position: absolute;
  width: 1px;
  height: 1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(0,0,0,0);
    }
  </style>

  <div class="hero">
    <img src="/images/hero.jpg" alt="2DCAT - Dark Synthpop duo from Washington D.C." class="hero-img" />
    <div class="hero-overlay"></div>
    <div class="hero-content">
      <p class="hero-tag">Washington D.C. &bull; Dark Synthpop</p>
      <h1>2DCAT<span class="sr-kw"> — Dark Synthpop & Darkwave</span></h1>
<p class="hero-sub">Analog-driven synthesizers. Commanding vocals. Music built for solitude and the dancefloor.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="bio-section">
    <p>
      2DCAT is a dark synthpop duo from Washington, D.C. Their music draws from darkwave, coldwave,
      minimal wave, and EBM traditions rooted in late 1970s and early 1980s European electronic music.
      Fronted by HAEZL, an acclaimed vocalist who has performed alongside Patti LaBelle, Cynthia Erivo,
      and Renée Fleming, and Johan, who designs and builds analog synthesizers and FPGA-based instruments
      from scratch, 2DCAT creates music that is melancholic, cinematic, and built for both the dancefloor
      and solitude.
    </p>
    <p>
      Their sound belongs to the Schwarze Szene and appeals to fans of Lebanon Hanover, Boy Harsher,
      Kite, NNHMN, Linea Aspera, Minuit Machine, Kontravoid, and Zanias. Based in Washington D.C.,
      2DCAT performs across North America and Europe.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div id="links" style="display:none"></div>
  <div id="email" style="display:none"></div>
  <script>
    if (window.location.hash === '#links') {
      window.location.href = '/links';
    }
    if (window.location.hash === '#email') {
      window.location.href = '/email.html';
    }
  </script>
</Base>